NotesRegister lists technical notes as an engineering drawing register (a revision table): date, note number, topic, title and standard, with topic filter chips and the latest or next planned note in a larger panel beside it.

- Data: block `"type": "register"` (`assets/src/blocks/register.js`). `topics: ["Standards", …]` (chip order), `items: [{t, topic, std, date, link, featured, d}]`. `t` title, `topic` one of `topics`, `std` the standard it reads, `link` a page id (the title links to it), `d` one line shown only in the featured panel. An item without `date` shows a mono "Planned" status: never invent a date, and placeholders stay placeholders.
- Featured: the item with `featured: true`, else the first item of the first topic. Labelled "Latest" when it has a date, "Next planned" when not. It also stays in the register (its number in `flow`).
- Markup: `.aq-notes-register` grid > `.aq-notes-register__filter` (`role="group"`, `button.aq-notes-register__chip` with `aria-pressed` and `data-topic`; "All" first, each with its count), a visually hidden `aria-live` count, `aside.aq-notes-register__feature` (mono `__flabel` strip, `h3.__ft`, `p.__fd`, one `.aq-tag`, the linked page's drawing as an aria-hidden `.aq-illustration` when it has one, `__go` "Applied on <page>"), `.aq-notes-register__reg` > `table.aq-notes-register__table` (rows `tr[data-topic]`, the title a `th scope="row"` whose link covers the row).
- Filtering is client-side: a chip hides the other rows (`hidden`) and shows every matching row even if folded; the fold button hides while a topic is chosen. "All" restores the fold.
- Desktop: chips across the top; panel (320 px) left with a `flow` top rule, register right in a `line-strong` frame, `line` hairlines between cells, mono `ink-muted` meta, sans `ink` titles, `flow-tint` on hover. Phones: chips scroll sideways in one line (44 px targets), the panel stacks above without its drawing, rows become two lines: title; topic · standard · status.
- Ground: navy by default (not in `LIGHT`); tokens only, so it reads the same on a light sheet with `ground: "light"`.
- Supports `fold: N` (first N rows under "All") and `fold_noun` ("Show all 24 notes"). Order items so the first topic leads.
- Not for documents a buyer receives (DocList) or for comparisons (CompareTable). In use on news.
